## Summary

| Dataset | Verdict | Used for |
|---|---|---|
| Endomondo (FitRec) | **Go, with a narrower question.** Only long-term users are in the data, so it cannot give retention or activation rates. | Lapses and returns among established members |
| HeartSteps V1 | **Go.** The randomization ran as designed. | The experiment readout |

## Endomondo: who is in the data?

The file holds 962\,190 workouts from 1\,364 users. 213 workouts (0\.02%) have impossible dates, before Endomondo launched in 2007 or after the data was collected, and are dropped.

The bigger finding is who was kept. The median user has 584\.5 workouts over 3\.4 years, and only 7 users have fewer than 10. Real app data always has many people who try the app a few times and leave. Their absence means the dataset was built from long-term users, so any retention rate measured here would be near 100% by construction.

